graded). Last healthy release: v5.0.0\n- payments-worker: running v3.4.0 (unhealthy). Last healthy release: v3.3.0\nThe deploy history doesn't show timestamps, so I can't tell which one was deployed this morning. Which should I roll back: payments-api, payments-worker, or both? Should the SEV2 incident cover both?", "context": {}}, {"t_ms": 271910, "event": "human_response", "actor": "human", "escalation": "esc1", "decision": "answer", "message": "It's payments-worker - the API errors are downstream of the worker.", "latency_ms": 254847, "hint": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "erred": false}, {"t_ms": 276092, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01GgR29AcB5KSgafW4GTwbm4", "tool": "rollback", "args": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 280092, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01GgR29AcB5KSgafW4GTwbm4", "tool": "rollback", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 280092, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GgR29AcB5KSgafW4GTwbm4", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 280092, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_012izVEZG5nryYJmuqrUiB9N", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "payments-worker v3.4.0 causing elevated errors; rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "After this morning's deploy of payments-worker v3.4.0, the service became unhealthy with an 18% error rate in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). payments-api (v5.1.0) is also showing an 18% error rate, which the owner says is downstream of the worker. We rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0, its last release that was healthy in production. Next: confirm the worker and payments-api recover.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "