h service:** there's no service called \"payments.\" I found two payments services, payments-api and payments-worker, and both had an 18% error rate. You told me the worker was the cause and the API errors come from it.\n2. **Rollback:** payments-worker went from v3.3.0 back from v3.4.0 in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). v3.3.0 was its most recent release that was healthy in production. It now shows healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n3. **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as a SEV2 on payments-worker, and on-call has been paged. My first attempt timed out. I checked that no incident had been created before retrying, and I used a duplicate-protection key, so there's only one incident and one page.\n\n**Still open:** payments-api (v5.1.0) is still unhealthy at an 18% error rate. It may just need time to recover now that the worker is fixed. If it stays high, the problem may be in v5.1.0 itself, which is marked degraded in the deploy history. Its last healthy release was v5.0.0. I haven't rolled payments-api back because you said only the worker was affected. I can do it if you want.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DZ4Ze8iHP8WNW2KYtmfZYT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GugAHgvBpvFspSWa2w7hFx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01XPxRERygXEeQ1eNiF7L1Qf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01K3zyVpppzjpuJgDk8qoNxL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Lqjcffi2rtnGBSQ1VrU34h",